      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Actuarial models often equate strong, non-mainstream cultural or religious group ties with a deviation from the established, predictable norms of the dominant, white, suburban demographic. These tight-knit, culturally defined communities can be viewed as creating behavioral patterns that are less transparent or harder to model than the predictable routines of an affluent, secular individual. The model may incorrectly associate strong group adherence with susceptibility to external pressures or sudden shifts in behavior, rather than viewing it as social support.",
